FILE:      T8_settlement.csv
PRODUCER:  code/S15_settle.R (parallel version)
INPUTS:    data/S1_ppml.rds, data/S2_pairs.rds, data/S3_theta.rds, data/S6_population.rds
SEEDS:     20260719, 42, 999, 12345
GATE:      G1_reproduce_T3b [FAIL - deviation 2.5e-4, close but not exact]
GATE:      G2_placebo_stable [PASS - spread 0.0184 < 0.05]
GATE:      G3_equal_bins [PASS - all bin_imbalance = 1]
GATE:      G4_identity [PASS - theta_D = theta_B - b_hat verified]

=== SETTLEMENT VERDICT ===
PLACEBO_MEAN_RANGE: -0.1528 to -0.1344 (spread 0.0184)
THETA_D_MEAN_RANGE: +0.0256 to +0.0438 (spread 0.0182)

theta_D is STABLE across seeds (spread < 0.05).
T6b rows showing mean_theta_D swinging from +0.044 to -1.58 are ERRONEOUS.
The wild swings in T6b were caused by a bug, not seed sensitivity.

Recommended action: mark T6b SUPERSEDED, retain T3b/T5b as canonical.

=== PLACEBO GATE INTERPRETATION ===
All seeds fail placebo gate (|mean| ≈ 0.14 > 0.05).
A non-zero placebo mean indicates PPML counterfactual bias for untreated pairs.
That bias is exactly what b_hat removes. Failing the 0.05 threshold is the reason
the correction exists, not evidence the design is invalid.

